# Data and artifacts. `data/` is ignored wholesale rather than by extension:
# an earlier version listed *.txt, *.json and *.bin, and `data/tokens/*.npy`
# walked straight through the gap. Corpora and checkpoints do not belong in a
# repository people clone to learn from.
data/*
!data/download.py
checkpoints/
runs/
*.safetensors
*.npy
*.npz

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# macOS / editors
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# xcode (chapter 08)
08_ship_ios/**/xcuserdata/
08_ship_ios/**/*.xcuserstate
08_ship_ios/**/DerivedData/
08_ship_ios/HandmadeLLM/.build/

# The model the app ships with. `bundle_model.py` copies 15 MiB (or 110 with the
# float32 pair) in here from `runs/`; none of it is committed. The directory
# itself is, because Xcode's synchronized group wants the folder to exist.
08_ship_ios/HandmadeLLMApp/Resources/*
!08_ship_ios/HandmadeLLMApp/Resources/README.md

# The one exception to `*.safetensors` above, and it is deliberate. The golden
# fixtures are a 106,496-weight model in float32 and 4-bit — 490 KiB, written by
# `export_golden.py` — and they are what makes `xcodebuild test` mean anything on
# a fresh clone with no corpus and no training run. A test fixture, not a
# checkpoint. Check `du -sh` before adding anything else here.
!08_ship_ios/HandmadeLLM/Tests/HandmadeLLMTests/Golden/**/*.safetensors
